                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25be4178-1f1a-30d7-95fc-041fa30fb56d",
                        "entry_id": "2a13df74-a59d-3579-8b9c-6b8efe96607f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom usuel d’Aleurites moluccanus, arbre tropical de la famille des Euphorbiaceae originaire de différentes zones du Pacifique (Indonésie, Malaisie, Nouvelle-Calédonie) et dont les drupes nommées noix de bancoul contiennent une amande utilisée pour faire une huile comestible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a15dab68-79a7-4b2a-b57e-ea320c4d9ca4",
                                "sense_id": "25be4178-1f1a-30d7-95fc-041fa30fb56d",
                                "text": "Dans une zone géographique donnée, si la forêt primaire a un caractère unique, les dégradations qui peuvent lui être infligées sont de formes et d’intensités variables, de sorte que la gamme des forêts secondaires est illimitée : … monocultures d’arbres à usages commerciaux, tecks, pins, palmiers à huile, bois d’aigle, girofliers ou bancouliers ; plantations clonales d’eucalyptus témoignant d’un paroxysme de volonté simplificatrice pour un rapide retour sur investissement ; brousses des bords de route, banales et tristes, dont on voit mal quel sera l’avenir, sauf à être envahies par les ruminants, puis par des graminées dans lesquelles le feu va passer chaque année, ruinant tout espoir de retour à la forêt d’origine."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "97db8bf5-eec7-4293-80d8-b63774400faa",
                        "source_entry_id": "2a13df74-a59d-3579-8b9c-6b8efe96607f",
                        "source_sense_id": "25be4178-1f1a-30d7-95fc-041fa30fb56d",
                        "target_lang_word": "candlenut",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "candlenut",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "004b8a5e-cf98-3548-9710-0db5bdd207d4",
                                        "entry_id": "6b4e2b69-f2e9-3aef-b310-2a63ad8ca119",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A flowering tree (Aleurites moluccana and Aleurites rockinghamensis) of the family Euphorbiaceae, also known as candleberry, Indian walnut, kemiri, varnish tree or kukui nut tree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cc8c644-6b05-43c1-a2c6-f282343b8cd3",
                                                "sense_id": "004b8a5e-cf98-3548-9710-0db5bdd207d4",
                                                "text": "In both respects, as I have already pointed out, they differed from the Polynesians who brought with them to their island homes not only their language but their agriculture, from the cradle of their race in the Malay Archipelago; cuttings of seedless breadfruit and of sugarcane, fleshy roots of taro and yams; even trees, like the Indian almond and the candlenut."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01f077a8-d1ec-3d44-a9d2-4896bd70dc32",
                                        "entry_id": "6b4e2b69-f2e9-3aef-b310-2a63ad8ca119",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The seed of this tree, used as a candle"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f4f043c-7acd-44ae-ac9a-d3676433b172",
                                                "sense_id": "01f077a8-d1ec-3d44-a9d2-4896bd70dc32",
                                                "text": "The scene under the candlenut torches was as familiar to us as the Ohio River of Uncle Tom to the small-town schoolboy; the meager rows of three-quarter naked Kanakas, yellow with saffron and blue with tattooer's ink; the old women in the background of sultry lights and enormous shadows compounding endless balls of popoi for the feast; the local and desceptered chieftain squatting on his hams and guarding the vanished gallon between his knees; this was all as it should have been."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
